      <h2 id="h-start">Your first ten minutes</h2>
      <p class="lede">Do these once, in this order, and OmniVEN will open on what matters to you.</p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><div><h3>Sign in with your work Google account</h3><p>Go to <b>omniven.cc</b> and choose <b>Sign in with Google</b>. Only <b>@39dollarglasses.com</b> accounts get in. Sessions last 16 hours, then you sign in again. If it says you don't have access, ask an admin to add you on the People page.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Start on Tasks</h3><p>You always land on the <b>Tasks</b> board: one column each for Leona, Chanley and Kaylie (and anyone else with open work), side by side. Your column holds your tasks, colored by brand (<b>39DollarGlasses</b>, <b>Ocusafe</b>, <b>Ocusleep</b>), plus the routines assigned to you for today, this week, month or quarter, in purple with a dashed edge. Tick either kind right there. Everything finished in the last 14 days is crossed out below the columns. Click the OmniVEN logo any time to come back here.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Filter to your brands</h3><p>The <b>All brands</b> button next to the search box opens the brand list (<b>39DollarGlasses, Ocusafe, Neurolux…</b>). Pick one and every tab filters to it at once; the button shows the brand in force. OmniVEN remembers your choice on this computer.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Star what you open most, and put it in your order</h3><p>Press <b>☆</b> next to any page title (Routines, Tasks, the action calendar, Help…), a tool category like <b>Affiliate</b>, a tool card, a brand page or an account. Stars appear in <b>My launchpad</b> above the tabs and at the top of <b>Jump to</b> (<kbd>⌘K</kbd>), on any device you sign in from. Press <b>Arrange</b> on My launchpad, then drag a star or use <b>‹ ›</b> to change the order. The <b>Recent</b> line fills in by itself.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Search everything from one box</h3><p>The search box above the tabs is an omni search. Type a few letters and a list drops down with matching <b>brands, pages, tool categories, tools, accounts, routines, tasks, action calendar items, bulletin posts</b> and your own sticky notes (admins also see people). Use <kbd>↑</kbd> <kbd>↓</kbd> and <kbd>Enter</kbd>, or click. The tab you're on filters as you type too, and the last line searches Help.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Learn one shortcut: <kbd>⌘K</kbd></h3><p>On Windows it's <kbd>Ctrl K</kbd>. Type a brand and platform, like <b>ocusafe insta</b>, and press Enter. Accounts and tools open in a new tab. Press <kbd>⇧</kbd><kbd>Enter</kbd> to star what's highlighted.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Ask for the logins you need</h3><p>On the <b>Access</b> tab or a brand page, press <b>Request access</b> on any tool or account and say why. An admin shares it through the password manager and marks it granted. You'll see <b>Requested</b>, then <b>✓ Granted</b>.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Open this week's action calendar</h3><p>Press <b>Calendar</b> in the top bar, or the progress strip at the top of Routines. It opens on the current week of the Q4 plan: what's due each day, for which brand, and what "done" looks like. Tick items as you finish them; the whole team sees the same checkmarks.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Make a sticky note for this week</h3><p>On <b>Sticky Notes</b>, create a colored note with your own to-dos. It sticks to the top right of every page, so you can tick items wherever you are. Press <b>Unstick</b> at the bottom of the note to put it back on the tab. Only you can see your notes. Nobody else can, admins included, and they never appear in logs.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Hand off work with a task</h3><p>On the <b>Tasks</b> tab, press <b>+ New task</b>. Write what needs doing, pick the person (you included), add a due date and details. Tick <b>Add to Hotlist</b> only if it's urgent: it pins the task to the top of everyone's page. Admins use the same form to add routines.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
